{
  "version": 121,
  "released": "2026-08-06",
  "changelog": "v121: local Telegram answers now receive the same warm acknowledgment as hosted Lifehug. `process-answer` first makes the answer file and any requested commit durable, then generates one 2–4 sentence, detail-specific reply through the canonical `answer-ack-prompt` and shared AI provider, and only then sends the optional adaptive follow-up. Provider, generation, and Telegram failures stay best-effort and never change answer success or suppress the follow-up; keyless agent-task mode remains immediate and receives no fake acknowledgment. A metadata-only ledger keyed by the durable `answer:{ID}` source id prevents confirmed duplicates, treats lost send responses as visibly ambiguous instead of blindly repeating them, and supports an explicit operator-confirmed retry. `answer-ack-status`, `answer-ack-retry`, and doctor expose recovery without ever logging or storing answer, prompt, generated message, or secret text.",
